{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"ROOT-CAUSE INVESTIGATION (rebar-debug) — db1c was PARTLY, not fully, fixed by d59e.\n\nVerified against origin/main @ 8ffdcea0d.\n\n## What d59e (99e22e4c2) already fixed\n\n- AC1 (a ticket whose description alone nears the budget still produces a verdict): DONE. `_MAX_CONTEXT_CHARS` is now 100,000 (`src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_recovery.py`), and `tests/unit/workflow/test_completion_recovery_oversized_d59e.py::test_a_real_blocked_ticket_now_reaches_a_verdict` is parametrized on ticket 2932's EXACT reported size (41,595 chars).\n- AC2 (recovery budget documented alongside the main pass, relationship stated): DONE at `docs/llm-framework.md:524-531`, including the criteria <= context invariant.\n\n## What was still live\n\n- AC3 (the error message must not recommend shortening the description without noting it invalidates the plan-review attestation): STILL LIVE. Confirmed at runtime — `recovery_failure_cause()` in `src/rebar/llm/failure.py:414-418` still emitted: 'so the recovery pass was refused before it ran — shorten the ticket's description/comments.'\n\nProven root cause: BOTH halves of that remedy are unactionable, for two different reasons, each contradicted by code already on main.\n\n1. description — `material_fingerprint()` at `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/pass1.py:715-732` hashes the description into the plan-review attestation ('a material edit invalidates the signature'). Editing it to clear the completion gate trips `require_plan_review_for_close`. The remedy for one close gate is a guaranteed failure of the other.\n2. comments — comments are explicitly NON-material (attestation-safe to edit), but the store is append-only: `src/rebar/_lib_writes.py:511` exposes `comment()` with NO delete or redact counterpart. That lever does not exist at all.\n\nCorroborating: d59e itself shipped a test whose docstring says the remedy 'could not be carried out', while leaving the message printing it unchanged.\n\n## On the reported NON-DETERMINISM — explained, not a separate defect\n\nRecovery is entered only when the PRIMARY pass raises a token-exhaustion `UnretryableOutputError` (`completion_recovery.py` `CompletionAgentStep.run` -> `_is_token_exhaustion`). Whether the primary exhausts is model-dependent, so the same ticket can take the recovery path on one attempt and not the next — exactly the attempt-2-fails / attempt-3-passes pattern reported. That is the fallback design, not a bug. With the cap at 100,000, entering recovery no longer means a refusal for any real ticket, so the flaky-refusal symptom is gone at its source.\n\n## Fix pushed\n\nGerrit change 1116 — https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1116\nConfined to `src/rebar/llm/failure.py` (message + docstring) plus a new test `tests/unit/test_close_gate_bound_remedy_db1c.py`. No bound, exception type, diagnostic key or control flow changed.\n\nNew operator message:\n'The ticket's context (100,001 chars) exceeds the bounded completion-recovery limit (100,000 chars), so the recovery pass was refused before it ran. The context cannot simply be made smaller: its comments are append-only (the store has no redaction operation), and its description is material, so editing it invalidates the plan-review attestation, which would then have to be re-earned. Its gate_error_v1 sidecar holds the full diagnostic.'\n\n## Evidence for AC4 (three consecutive attempts, identical content)\n\nDriving `CompletionAgentStep` with a 41,595-char context (ticket 2932's size) three times with byte-identical content: verdicts ['PASS', 'PASS', 'PASS']. Under the pre-d59e 24,000 cap this size was refused before the pass ran.\n\nTest discipline: the new test was confirmed RED on both bug assertions before any fix existed, held out from the implementing subagent, and returned to RED under a mutation restoring the old literal. Full unit suite after: 6274 passed, 20 skipped. lint + typecheck clean.\n\nSibling sweep for the bug class ('operator remedy names an unreachable lever'): no other instance in `src/` outside the reconciler surface."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785517268546139001,"uuid":"06fcee63-7000-486f-a79e-46448429de54"}